{
 "about": "KernelCost (src/felizjueves/lower.py, #284) of the fused HGP kernel (kernel_f.build_f_kernel, #282) for milestone 12's 21 classes, beside hgp.cost's FLOP triple (#276) for the same class. 'nest' is every computing statement (Decl with init, Assign, WarpReduce, AtomicAdd) by its enclosing For loops, outermost first; 'tiers' maps it with lower.tiered under 'loops': inside the per-quartet loop k and both primitive loops K4, one K2, none K0; outside k (per block: the staging copy, the bra reads) 'outside'. The tiers sum to n_instructions, the flat static count. STATEMENTS, NOT FLOPS: KernelCost counts IR statements and hgp.cost counts FLOPs, so the two are compared per class, never equated or merged; hgp.cost's K2 is the pair geometry the kernel receives pre-staged (its K2 statements are the ket row's loads). 'carried' is the most loop-carried values of one For (the K_CD loop's boundary accumulators), and peak_live >= carried by lower.py's loop model. KernelCost feeds no floor. Recorded before #283's six-block digestion: its K4 and K2 tiers are digestion-independent and test/test_lower.py holds them equal to the kernel; K0, 'outside', peak_live and n_instructions are this snapshot's, regenerated with `PYTHONPATH=src uv run python test/test_lower.py --write-f`.",
